I started with a chaotic elf priest of Loki. I proceeded by going down a 
few levels and then hitting the mines first. People will probably 
disagree with this strategy, pointing out that the survival rate is 
better if you go to Sokoban first, but I like having the opportunity to 
get a decent weapon and maybe a wish first.

As it turns out, I managed to find a blessed magic lamp in a hardware 
store, which I used to get blessed gray dragon scale mail. I also found 
a few decent spellbooks, including detect treasure. Since the priest was 
generated with a spellbook of clairvoyance, I managed to enhance 
divination spells along the way. This came in handy.

My cat and I went to the bottom of mines first, to get the luckstone. 
(It was the end with the Gnome King's potion stash, but I didn't bother 
with it at first, wanting to spend as little time at mine end as 
possible.) My large cat killed a unicorn as we went down - grabbed the 
horn and blessed it.

I cleared out Sokoban and got a bag of holding, which I blessed. So far 
so good.

As I went down I found a series of thronerooms, which yielded an 
unprecedented number of wishes. I wished for speed boots from the first 
one, and then gauntets of power from the next (I was getting paranoid of 
c corpses while blind). I didn't have reflection yet, which concerned 
me, but I figured I'd find it on Medusa's island.

Using my detect treasure spell, I also found each and every gold vault 
on the way down. One of them had the entrance to Ft. Ludios. Since I 
didn't have reflection I left it for later. I found lots of spellbooks, 
including a spellbook of remove curse.

I fought Medusa blindfolded and got the shield of reflection from the 
statue of Perseus. I didn't know if Medusa's corpse would stone me, so I 
kept my blindfold on and proceeded down to the castle level. 
Interestingly there was a temple between the levels, where I made 
sizable donations for protection.

The castle level yielded a fully charged WoW. Since I already found a 
scroll of charging, I used the first 3 wishes for a +2 tshirt, an amulet 
of life saving and a magic marker. The throne on the level yielded yet 
another wish, which I used for a cursed scroll of genocide (which 
wouldn't break conduct).

I nurse danced in Sokoban to get my HP up to about 180, and fixed all my 
gear. I cleared out Ft. Ludios, and paid for more protection.

At this point I decided to go on the quest (my AC was around -25). I ate 
some wraith corpses to get to around lvl 17 and Nalzok provided no 
meaningful challenge.

I prayed at an altar for the stealth and speed intrinsics, and got my 
armor powered up. I charged a ring of protection up to +4. My AC wound 
up to be at -50. Loki finally condescended to give me an artifact weapon 
and crowned me.

In the valley of the dead I was lucky enough to find a spellbook of 
magic mapping. I used it to map all the levels as I went through them, 
which helped me to avoid liches and mind flayers.

Everything was A OK until Orcus Town. The stairs up to Vlad's Tower was 
there, so I killed Vlad and took the candleabrum as well as a second 
amulet of life saving. Orcus decided to be his usual pain in the rear 
self, and summoned both Yeenoghu and Demogorgon. Two arch liches also 
decided to appear, along with a massive horde of monsters. Goodbye 1st AoLS.

I retreated to Vlad's Tower, where the demon lords didnt follow. I had 
to think of some way to kill them. The liches had already managed to 
unbless my unicorn horn and make it less effective to Demogorgon's 
sickness attacks and I couldn't well keep blessing it with potions of 
holy water from my sack while ill in the middle of combat. I rested in 
Vlad's tower until my HP were at full, and then used a cursed wand of 
create monster to try and produce a cockatrice. It didn't work, but one 
was lurking on the level anyway. I killed it and wielded the corpse, 
turning the arch liches and demon lords to stone.

I went back up to minetown to get candles and my remove curse spellbook 
(I left it in a stash in Sokoban). On the way I met a friendly nurse in 
the Valley of the Dead. As I was naked and weaponless, a vrock happened 
along and gated in some of his friends, who gated in their friends. I 
was surrounded before I could get my armor back on and reduced to 0 hp. 
Goodbye AoLS #2. Let this be a lesson for the future - no nurse dancing 
in hell.

With no lifesaving amulets left, I went back to minetown and got some 
candles. I also took the opportunity to loot the Gnome King's wine 
cellar for booze potions (handy when I want to be confused). Taking any 
spellbooks from my stashes I thought I might need, I proceeded 
cautiously down.

The vibrating square was surprising easy to find; I started looking at 
the opposite end of the maze from where I came down and there it was. 
Rodney's zoo yielded more W corpses, as well as a potion of gain level. 
My level went up to 24. Rodney was not happy when I produced a wand of 
death and blasted him in the face. He was equally unhappy about it on 
the 8 succeeding times I did it to him.

The high priest of Moloch and two Rodneys went down to WoD attacks. I 
grabbed the amulet (and a fake amulet), IDed them to find the correct 
one, #named it and ran like hell.

The elemental planes were simple - I had saved up 4 scrolls of gold 
detection and had booze potions. I was mostly concerned about being 
cursed (I had 14 potions of holy water in my sack, and an extra 
spellbook of remove curse just in case).

The Astral Plane was a fiasco. I went up the middle, avoiding Famine by 
leaving him behind a wall of insects the priests had summoned. Odin's 
temple was in the middle. OK, since death was on the left, I decided to 
go right, which was Tyr's temple. I used my last potion of full healing 
trying to get out (and almost died - I had 39hp surrounded by tough 
enemies). The angel Loki sent me was useless.

OK, so I went right, to the last temple, with death directly between me 
and the altar. I made furious use of a blessed wand of teleportation to 
teleport enemies away from around me and tried to keep insects and enemy 
priests between death and myself. Death finally went around me in an 
effort to get to me and I blasted everyone in front of me with the last 
charges of my death wands. I sandbagged death, got to the altar, and 
sacrificed the amulet.

Woohoo! Time for a drink!


